Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:54:38 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] AWindow: keep the window size when a vout unregisters

The size is the surface's, and the surface outlives the vout. Forgetting
it on unregister left the next vout with nothing to replay when it
registered, and nothing else sends it again until the surface changes.
A vout with no window size places the picture at the source size from
the top-left corner: switching from a 1080p title to a 640x360 one
showed a small picture in the corner of an otherwise green surface.

detachViews still forgets it, as the surface is gone then.
---
 libvlc/src/main/java/org/videolan/libvlc/AWindow.java | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libvlc/src/main/java/org/videolan/libvlc/AWindow.java b/libvlc/src/main/java/org/videolan/libvlc/AWindow.java
index 382f2a2..23d900e 100644
--- a/libvlc/src/main/java/org/videolan/libvlc/AWindow.java
+++ b/libvlc/src/main/java/org/videolan/libvlc/AWindow.java
@@ -528,8 +528,6 @@ public class AWindow implements IVLCVout {
             if (mCallbackNativeHandle == 0)
                 throw new IllegalArgumentException("unregister called when not registered");
             mCallbackNativeHandle = 0;
-            mWindowWidth = -1;
-            mWindowHeight = -1;
         }
     }
 
